<newsitem itemid="130165" id="root" date="1996-10-21" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kohler lifts yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Kohler lifts yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr</p>
<p>    - attrib (cts)	  48.2	  vs 40.1</p>
<p>    - pre abnormals (cts) 47.2	  vs 40.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)  9.4 making 15.8	  vs 14.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   146.6	 vs 119.4</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	  1.3 gain    vs 1.4 charge</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   207.9	 vs 178.6</p>
<p>    Tax			 61.2	  vs 55.1</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   4.1	   vs 30.5</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,335.5     vs 3,005.2</p>
<p>Div payable December 9</p>
<p>on register November 15</p>
<p>Full name: Kohler Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast earnings for paper and packaging company Kohler between 46 and 47.1 cents a share with a consensus 46.5 cents. They had expected a dividend of 16 cents.</p>
<p>Lower volumes in the packaging industry were likely to prevail for some time, the company said, but the outlook for agriculture appeared good. It predicted continued real growth in earnings.</p>
<p>Abnormal items reflect profits on sale of businesses and charges for discontinued operations.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
